     1,
     "\nThree packages were updated last week.<br>\n<a style=\"font-weight:bold\" href=\"https://CRAN.R-project.org/package=secr\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://CRAN.R-project.org/package%3Dsecr&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792486192672000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1Lf8zo75fGY8c7N0Xp6ZUL\">secr</a> 5.2.4 has mostly minor <a href=\"https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/secr/NEWS\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/secr/NEWS&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792486192673000&amp;usg=AOvVaw280PpYwjcrm94uRwfWPEgY\">changes</a><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">.</span>\nSimulation of activity centres with sim.popn() allows fixed-N when\nmodel2D uses rLGCP or rThomas, building on changes in the spatstat\npackage.<a style=\"font-weight:bold\" href=\"https://CRAN.R-project.org/package=secrdesign\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://CRAN.R-project.org/package%3Dsecrdesign&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792486192673000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0gPAtv5y0U8qrSXHlpzDP1\"><br>\nsecrdesign</a> 2.10.0 adds functions to simulate movement paths from an\nOrnstein-Uhlenbeck process (simOU), and hence to simulate detections at\npoint detectors that are serially correlated in space (simOU.capthist).\nThese functions are exercised in the vignette available <a href=\"https://www.otago.ac.nz/density/pdfs/secrdesign-vignette.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.otago.ac.nz/density/pdfs/secrdesign-vignette.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792486192673000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1ZxkmVh_0jaYEw5mn_x4-d\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">here</span></a>.<br>\n<a style=\"font-weight:bold\" href=\"https://CRAN.R-project.org/package=ipsecr\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://CRAN.R-project.org/package%3Dipsecr&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792486192673000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2VXIcZ90ilrDET_TfNAc7r\">ipsecr</a> 1.4.4 is most interesting for a new example in the <a href=\"https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/ipsecr/vignettes/ipsecr-vignette.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/ipsecr/vignettes/ipsecr-vignette.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792486192673000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0U2cazc6d3c2IkAt-nMVIq\">vignette</a> that implements an idea from Kodi et al. (2024 MEE 15:1060-1070) for reducing bias due to identification errors.\n\n<br>"
